A||N||6||firstfiero|| odd fan problem?||||5||
Z||000000||firstfiero||03-25-2001||01:23 PM||||    Got a strange one...Got into my car today and when I shut it off I herd something clicking loudly. Pop the hood and find that for some reason the fan is now hitting the housing at the to of the fan. It's like the plastic warped a little or something. Is this one of those strange things typical to a fiero? should I try to bend it back or loosen the housing? <P>------------------<BR>'86 fiero Se<BR>    Todd<BR>NO MR. RICER STICKERS DON'T MAKE YOU FASTER!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||03-25-2001||01:37 PM||||This is common to plastic fans.<P>Make sure the fan motor is where it belongs and tight to the bracket. If the motor got out of place the fan could drag.<P>If the fan or frame are warped then there's not allot you can do. The plastics involved usually don't tolerate someone trying to bend them. You might could shave the frame to eliminate the spot thats rubbing.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 03-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||03-25-2001||01:40 PM||||Every Fiero that I have ever had has that problem. Usually a couple of flat washers under where the fan mounts to the core support will twist the housing enough to keep it from rubbing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||firstfiero||03-25-2001||01:50 PM||||   Thanks, I think thats what I'll do. Just shave the top of the fan down. <P>------------------<BR>'86 fiero Se<BR>    Todd<BR>NO MR. RICER STICKERS DON'T MAKE YOU FASTER!!!||||reg||14
Z||000004||firstfiero||03-25-2001||01:52 PM||||   That's not a bad idea either.....I'll try that first.<P>------------------<BR>'86 fiero Se<BR>    Todd<BR>NO MR. RICER STICKERS DON'T MAKE YOU FASTER!!!||||reg||14
Z||000005||firstfiero||03-25-2001||06:04 PM||||   easy fix....Took the two top screws out of the housing...put some washers in between the housing and the what screwed to and then tightened it up...perfect!! thanks<P>------------------<BR>'86 fiero Se<BR>    Todd<BR>NO MR. RICER STICKERS DON'T MAKE YOU FASTER!!!||||reg||14
Z||000006||ka4nkf||03-26-2001||12:40 AM||||If you shave the fan blades down, you better make sure that you take the same amount off of each blade or you will have a vibrating fan.||||reg||1
